<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE nrol-136 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 NROL-136 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs family knots + assumed orbit): vertical rise 13.98 s, kick 1.086 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400 fixed, payload 8000 kg FIXED ASSUMPTION (not a fitted parameter),
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.4275-0.001097*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
ILLUSTRATIVE. PRE-FLIGHT. NROL-136, fifteenth NRO proliferated-architecture batch, Falcon 9 from SLC-4E. LL2 id 951a341f-236b-42fe-a667-4ab2fcf36eac, status Go, NET 2026-11-21T12:30:00Z (Sat 21 Nov 4:30 a.m. PST), window 12:30-13:00Z. SpaceX nrol136 page: 30-minute window opens 4:30 a.m. PT, backup Sunday 22 Nov 4:16 a.m. PT, booster 14th flight, landing LZ-4. FAA advisory primary 21 Nov 1230-1343Z.
Published timeline (SpaceX nrol136, checked 2026-11-18): Max-Q 1:02, MECO 2:11, stage sep 2:14, SES-1 2:22, fairing 2:59, boostback 2:27-3:22, entry 5:53-6:10, landing burn 7:09, LZ-4 landing 7:34. SECO, orbit and deploy are NOT published.
INFERRED/ASSUMED: SECO-1 at T+510 s (near a full S2 load; the time itself is not published) and a 310 x 425 km parking orbit borrowed from prior proliferated batches, not from an NROL-136 source. Azimuth 155.15 deg is from LNM 58668 Hazard Area A. File ends 2 revs after cutoff (deploy unpublished). There is no prior NROL Vandenberg trajectory in this repo; USSF-317 is a different, droneship profile.
Target (see launch config): insertion 310 km, apoapsis 425 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 155.15 deg; payload 8000 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-21T12:30:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (SpaceX publishes no SECO, restart or deploy time for NROL-136; propagated 2 revs on the inferred insertion orbit). From insertion T+510.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 91.90 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11538 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 309.93 km, osculating 305.8 x 429.4 km, i 69.046 deg.</description>
